From: RockOS <rockos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] sandbox: fix SYS_SECCOMP clash with glibc >= 2.36

glibc 2.36+ defines SYS_SECCOMP as an enum constant in
<bits/siginfo-consts.h> (via <signal.h>). Chromium's linux_seccomp.h
falls back to #define SYS_SECCOMP 1, which collides when this header
is included before <signal.h> (the later glibc enum line expands the
macro). Include <signal.h> first so glibc's definition always wins
and the #ifndef below becomes a no-op in both include orders.

--- a/chromium/sandbox/linux/system_headers/linux_seccomp.h
+++ b/chromium/sandbox/linux/system_headers/linux_seccomp.h
@@ -7,6 +7,11 @@
 
 #include <stdint.h>
 
+// glibc >= 2.36 defines SYS_SECCOMP as an enum constant in
+// <bits/siginfo-consts.h> (via <signal.h>). Include it first so the
+// fallback define below sees it and does not redefine the enum constant.
+#include <signal.h>
+
 #include "build/build_config.h"
 
 #if !defined(OS_NACL_NONSFI)
